# The standard-cell library arrives as a pinned stdcells release and USED to be
# fetched at CI time and never committed (see PLAN.md, "Library consumption:
# pinned"). It is now COMMITTED, because as of 2026-07-25 the TinyTapeout
# submission is built from the ALL-OWN netlist and an artifact built from this
# repository can only use files that are IN this repository — a fetch step is
# not something the TT flow runs. Leaving it ignored would have silently
# defeated the blocker-1 fix: the config would reference lib/ files that do not
# exist for anyone but us.
# The pin is still authoritative: tools/verify_lib.py checks the committed bytes
# against lib.lock offline on every gds run, and tools/fetch_lib.py remains the
# only way to move the pin.
# lib/  <- deliberately NOT ignored any more
harden/runs/
harden/*.ys
harden/*.log
pdk-root/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
